// What <radiusoffset> does to a component of each class that has the element, as OpenRocket's
// RadiusPositionSetter does it. kJava holds OpenRocket's answers (the probe SpecialSetterProbe of
// tier 9b, part R2; see SetterTestSupport.h): the method and the offset (getRadiusMethod,
// getRadiusOffset) after the elements of a row, and the warnings. The last rows apply the
// setter by hand to a component it is not for, which no file does.

